 Q4. Defect Severity and Priority

1. Defect A – App Crashes on Place Order

- Severity: Critical
- Priority: High
- Reason: The application crashes when users try to place an order, affecting approximately 30% of users. 
It directly impacts the main functionality of the application and must be fixed immediately.

2. Defect B – Restaurant Logo Misalignment

- Severity: Minor
- Priority: Low
- Reason: The restaurant logo is slightly misaligned only on the iPhone SE model.
It does not affect the main functionality of the application, so it can be fixed later.

3. Difference between Severity and Priority:

Severity describes how seriously a defect affects the application, whereas Priority describes how quickly the defect should be fixed.
Defect A : has Critical severity and High priority because users cannot place orders.
Defect B : has Minor severity and Low priority because it only affects the visual appearance of the logo.

4. Which defect should be fixed first?

Defect A should be fixed first because the application crashes during order placement and affects approximately 30% of users.
It directly impacts the business and user experience. Therefore, the development team should give it the highest priority before release.
